From 7228f28079efb1c0df9453ac5c1a3cb49a3f3838 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 372/488] soh: name the 29 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_rl.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 29 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Rl/z_en_rl.c.

  * func_80AE72D0 -> EnRl_UpdateEyes
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs the blink timer and clamps the eye
    texture index to the three sEyeTextures entries

  * func_80AE7358 -> EnRl_SetupFadedOut
    deduced, confidence HIGH: loops the idle animation and drops to action 4
    with nothing drawn and no shadow

  * func_80AE73D8 -> EnRl_WatchCutsceneEnd
    deduced, confidence HIGH: latches while a cutscene runs and, on its end,
    fades the params 2 Rauru out

  * func_80AE744C -> EnRl_UpdateBgCheck
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs Actor_UpdateBgCheckInfo with Rauru's
    dimensions

  * func_80AE74B4 -> EnRl_IsCueAction
    deduced, confidence HIGH: true when the given cue channel is live and
    sitting on the caller's action id

  * func_80AE74FC -> EnRl_IsNotCueAction
    deduced, confidence HIGH: true when that cue channel is live and on any
    action other than the caller's

  * func_80AE7544 -> EnRl_InitSkelAnime
    deduced, confidence HIGH: builds the skeleton on the idle animation

  * func_80AE7590 -> EnRl_GiveLightMedallion
    deduced, confidence HIGH: in the Chamber of the Sages on cue 6 action 2,
    spawns the medallion effect above the player and grants
    ITEM_MEDALLION_LIGHT once

  * func_80AE7668 -> EnRl_SetupChamberScene
    deduced, confidence GUESS: turns the player around to face Rauru and
    moves to action 1 with the opaque draw; the scene it opens is inferred
    from the actions that follow

  * func_80AE7698 -> EnRl_WaitForGestureCue
    deduced, confidence GUESS: waits for cue 0 to reach action 3 and then
    plays object_rl_Anim_00040C once; the animation's content is not
    established beyond being the lead-in to the looping one

  * func_80AE772C -> EnRl_CheckGestureDone
    deduced, confidence HIGH: on that animation finishing, loops
    object_rl_Anim_000830 and advances to action 3

  * func_80AE7798 -> EnRl_Action0
    deduced, confidence HIGH: action 0: opens the chamber scene straight
    away

  * func_80AE77B8 -> EnRl_Action1
    deduced, confidence HIGH: action 1: bg check, animation and eyes while
    waiting for the gesture cue

  * func_80AE77F8 -> EnRl_Action2
    deduced, confidence HIGH: action 2: plays the gesture out and moves to
    the looping animation

  * func_80AE7838 -> EnRl_Action3
    deduced, confidence HIGH: action 3: the medallion hand-over step

  * func_80AE7878 -> EnRl_InitSkelAnimeHidden
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the params 2 init: builds the skeleton, starts
    at action 4 and hides the shadow

  * func_80AE78D4 -> EnRl_SpawnLightBall
    deduced, confidence HIGH: spawns the params 5 DEMO_6K light effect above
    Rauru

  * func_80AE7954 -> EnRl_WaitForAppearCue
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits for cue 0 action 4, then starts the
    translucent fade-in from zero alpha

  * func_80AE79A4 -> EnRl_FadeInOut
    deduced, confidence HIGH: ramps alpha and shadow alpha up while the cue
    holds and back down when it does not, switching draw mode at each end

  * func_80AE7AF8 -> EnRl_CheckGestureOrFade
    deduced, confidence GUESS: branches between starting the gesture
    animation and fading fully in with the light ball; named for the two
    outcomes rather than an identified beat of the scene

  * func_80AE7BF8 -> EnRl_CheckGestureDone2
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the action 6 twin of EnRl_CheckGestureDone,
    ending at action 7 instead of 3

  * func_80AE7C64 -> EnRl_Action4
    deduced, confidence HIGH: action 4: waits for the appear cue and watches
    for the cutscene ending

  * func_80AE7C94 -> EnRl_Action5
    deduced, confidence HIGH: action 5: runs the alpha fade with the
    animation and eyes

  * func_80AE7CE8 -> EnRl_Action6
    deduced, confidence HIGH: action 6: plays the gesture out into the
    looping animation

  * func_80AE7D40 -> EnRl_Action7
    deduced, confidence HIGH: action 7: the looping state, watching for the
    next gesture or a fade back

  * func_80AE7D94 -> EnRl_DrawXlu
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draw config 2: draws the skeleton
    translucently at the current alpha

  * func_80AE7FD0 -> EnRl_DrawNothing
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draw config 0: draws nothing

  * func_80AE7FDC -> EnRl_DrawOpa
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draw config 1: draws the skeleton opaque at
    full alpha

  * D_80AE81A0 -> sEyeTextures
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the three eye textures indexed by the blink
    counter

